[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise.
They come from three problems, and the parser fix closed only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: parser fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales),
hint won't fix (booking-v3 form retired). Nothing has fixed shift: its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: 'https://github.com/krukkrz/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/krukkrz/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2', shift: 'https://github.com/krukkrz/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3' }} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and these tenants write the day
  first. 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names. **Fixed.**
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, but it reads the date
  the tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint tells them, and the form swaps it. Only
  form reports from booking-v3 tenants. The parser fix does not touch it. **Won't fix:** the
  booking-v3 form is retired.
- **`shift`**: the date is right and the day moves by one. Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May,
  a meeting reaches Lisbon on Tuesday and Toronto on Monday, an invite arrives before its booking.
  That is a time-zone conversion, not a swap of day and month, so neither change above ends it.
  **Open.**

## How the count was made

- One report per id: the export repeats some reports, and `uniqueById` drops the copies.
- The cause comes from the tenant, not from intake. Intake tags from the reporter's browser, so
  its `hint` and `parser` tags disagree with the cause in both directions (the "intake tagged as"
  column).
- The `shift` reports are the ones the desk itself read as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`).
  They stay counted under `parser`, where their tenant files them, as in the desk's own view, and
  they are a problem of their own too. So the rows add up to more than the reports. The logic is
  in `src/lib/kb/problems.ts`.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. Every
report here has a subject about a wrong date, so three bugs with the same symptom became one
ticket. The decision accepted that cost for different subjects about one bug. It did not plan
for one subject over different bugs.

